flow — `secrets.NTFY_TOPIC` may be empty (fork PRs, unset secret): flows to the named-absence green path; no bypass reads; shell interpolation of `${{ github.event.repository.default_branch }}` into `run` is an inherited injection-shaped pattern (admin-controlled value only), unfixed.\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER: classified 11 of 11. (1) missing argv gate → true boundary (red). (2) ZERO_SHA head / branch deletion → true boundary, receipted (receipt 4, commits=0 green). (3) ZERO_SHA base + missing newBranchBase arg → true boundary (red), receipted (receipt 5). (4) merge-base effectiveBase computation → producer-fix of the storm bug, receipted (receipt 5: 2026→1). (5) verifyCommit head/base/default-branch gates → true boundary (red), receipted (receipt 4). (6) runGit spawn-error/nonzero-exit/maxBuffer guards → true boundary (red); maxBuffer overflow unreachability NOT receipted (no >10MB diff test). (7) `--diff-merges=first-parent` → producer-fix for git 2.53 empty diff-tree, receipted (receipt 6). (8) NTFY_TOPIC-absent green fallback → true boundary, contract-mandated named absence, receipted (receipts 2, 6). (9) HTTP non-2xx guard → true boundary (red), code-receipt only, NO test receipt. (10) timeout/error handlers → true boundary (red), NO test receipt. (11) main().catch internal-error → true boundary (red), NO test receipt.\nALLEGATIONS: A1 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — kimi review omits every required doctrine section and performs no guard classification. A2 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — HTTP-red path (guards 9/10) and internal-error path (11) have zero test receipts; supported only by code reading. A3 SUBSTANTIVE/TESTIMONY — routine force-pushes of main (mandated by CLAUDE.md git rules) will present an unfetched `github.event.before`, producing malfunction red on every force-push; contract-literal (\"git/range malfunction red\") but operationally noisy; needs Trey awareness, not a break. A4 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — default_branch shell interpolation in workflow run block, admin-controlled, low risk. A5 MECHANICAL/RECEIPT — rev-list without `--first-parent` means a merge push re-notifies every merged commit already notified on the PR event; duplicate noise, contract-compliant (\"every commit\"), detection-only.\nSUBSTANTIVE RESOLUTION: none — A3 is contract-compliant as written; it is surfaced as operator awareness in NEXT_CHECK, not a non-convergence requiring Trey adjudication of the artifact itself.\nWHAT I EXAMINED: full verbatim script (222 lines) and workflow (40 lines) from the prompt; SHA-attested evidence manifest; trusted receipts 1–8; kimi's prior review; Ruling 9 contract text; CLAUDE.md git rules for operational context.\nDID NOT EXAMINE: live ntfy delivery (no topic, forced buzz pending); HTTP non-2xx/timeout behavior under real execution; force-push event behavior in actual GitHub Actions; git version on the CI runner vs the 2.53.0 receipt environment; repo state at parent 4ac6d010 (no repo tools); whether `secrets.NTFY_TOPIC` is actually configured in the GitHub repo.\nASSUMED: host-attested receipts 1–8 are authentic trusted-path receipts (sandbox tests treated as non-authoritative per instruction); the SHA256-manifested excerpts match the verbatim text in the prompt; `actions/checkout@v4 fetch-depth: 0` fetches all refs such that PR base/head SHAs resolve; GitHub-supplied SHAs are 40-hex and shell-safe; ntfy.sh honors `Priority: max` header (unverified live)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14867,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14867},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[REDACTED]","uuid":"[REDACTED]","timestamp":"2026-09-02T05:32:01.761Z","request_id":"req_011Cee4bZuzmB9bZRDp1EeAt"}
